    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> was crowned the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> of All <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in January 1547.</li><li>It conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> khanates, crossed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> to the Pacific and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> and left-bank <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> in 1667.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a>’s reforms and victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> turned it into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> in 1721.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Russian explorers reached the Pacific at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-okhotsk">Sea of Okhotsk</a> in 1639, less than sixty years after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yermak-timofeyevich">Yermak</a>’s cossacks first crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-mountains">Urals</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

